{"task_id": "Mbpp/6", "solution": "def differ_At_One_Bit_Pos(num1: int, num2: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Check if two numbers differ at exactly one bit position.\n    \"\"\"\n    xor_result = num1 ^ num2\n    \n    # Count the number of set bits (1s) in the XOR result using Brian Kernighan's algorithm.\n    count = 0\n    while xor_result > 0:\n        xor_result &= (xor_result - 1)\n        count += 1\n    \n    return count == 1"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/3", "solution": "def is_not_prime(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given number is not prime.\n    Returns True if the number is not prime (composite), False if prime.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number <= 1:\n        return True\n    if number == 2:\n        return False\n    if number % 2 == 0:\n        return True\n    \n    # Check for divisibility by odd numbers up to the square root\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= number:\n        if number % i == 0:\n            return True\n        i += 2\n            \n    return False"}
