{"task_id": "Mbpp/12", "solution": "def sort_matrix(matrix):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a given matrix in ascending order according to the sum of its rows.\n    Uses a stable sort to preserve original order for rows with equal sums.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Calculate row sums and pair each row with its sum\n    rows_with_sums = []\n    for row in matrix:\n        row_sum = sum(row)\n        rows_with_sums.append((row_sum, row))\n\n    # Sort the pairs based on the row sum (first element of the tuple)\n    rows_with_sums.sort(key=lambda x: x[0])\n\n    # Extract the sorted rows\n    sorted_matrix = [row for _, row in rows_with_sums]\n\n    return sorted_matrix"}
