{"task_id": "Mbpp/61", "solution": "def count_Substrings(s):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of substrings in 's' where the sum of digits equals the substring's length.\n    This function iterates through all possible substrings, calculates their digit sum,\n    and increments a counter if the sum matches the substring's length.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    n = len(s)\n\n    # Iterate through all possible starting positions\n    for i in range(n):\n        # Iterate through all possible ending positions\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            substring = s[i : j + 1]\n            current_length = len(substring)\n            digit_sum = 0\n            \n            # Calculate the sum of digits for the current substring\n            for char in substring:\n                digit_sum += int(char)\n            \n            # Check if the sum of digits equals the substring's length\n            if digit_sum == current_length:\n                count += 1\n                \n    return count"}
