{"task_id": "Mbpp/63", "solution": "def _calculate_difference(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate absolute difference between two numeric values.\n    \"\"\"\n    return abs(a - b)\n\ndef _validate_input(tuples):\n    \"\"\"\n    Validate input format and content.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tuples, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    if not tuples:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n\n    for i, item in enumerate(tuples):\n        if not isinstance(item, tuple):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Element at index {i} must be a tuple.\")\n        if len(item) != 2:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Tuple at index {i} must contain exactly two elements.\")\n        if not (isinstance(item[0], (int, float)) and isinstance(item[1], (int, float))):\n            raise TypeError(f\"Elements in tuple at index {i} must be numeric.\")\n\ndef max_difference(tuples):\n    \"\"\"\n    Find the maximum difference between available pairs in the given tuple list.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_input(tuples)\n\n    # Initialize max_diff_val with the difference of the first tuple\n    first_tuple = tuples[0]\n    max_diff_val = _calculate_difference(first_tuple[0], first_tuple[1])\n\n    # Iterate through the rest of the tuples to find the maximum difference\n    for i in range(1, len(tuples)):\n        a, b = tuples[i]\n        current_diff = _calculate_difference(a, b)\n        if current_diff > max_diff_val:\n            max_diff_val = current_diff\n\n    return max_diff_val"}
