{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence using memoization.\n    The sequence is defined by P(1) = 1, P(2) = 1, and P(n) = P(P(n-1)) + P(n-P(n-1)) for n > 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a positive integer.\")\n    if n == 1 or n == 2:\n        return 1\n\n    # dp array to store calculated sequence values, indexed from 1\n    dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n    dp[1] = 1\n    dp[2] = 1\n\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        dp[i] = dp[dp[i-1]] + dp[i-dp[i-1]]\n\n    return dp[n]"}
