{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number is undulating, meaning it alternates between exactly two different digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    str_num = str(number)\n\n    # An undulating number must have at least two digits.\n    if len(str_num) < 2:\n        return False\n\n    # Extract digits from the number.\n    digits = [int(d) for d in str_num]\n\n    # Determine the unique digits present.\n    distinct_digits = set(digits)\n\n    # An undulating number must use exactly two different digits.\n    if len(distinct_digits) != 2:\n        return False\n\n    # Validate the alternating pattern: consecutive digits must always be different.\n    for i in range(1, len(digits)):\n        if digits[i] == digits[i-1]:\n            return False # Found identical consecutive digits, so it's not undulating.\n\n    # If all checks pass, the number is undulating.\n    return True"}
