{"task_id": "Mbpp/166", "solution": "from typing import List\n\ndef find_even_pair(numbers: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of pairs of integers in a list that XOR to an even number.\n    A pair (numbers[i], numbers[j]) is considered for i < j.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    n = len(numbers)\n\n    # Iterate through all unique pairs (i, j) where i < j\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            # Calculate the XOR result for the pair\n            xor_result = numbers[i] ^ numbers[j]\n\n            # Check if the XOR result is even\n            if xor_result % 2 == 0:\n                count += 1\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/170", "solution": "def sum_range_list(numbers_list, start_index, end_index):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of numbers in a list within a specified range of indices (inclusive).\n    Returns 0 if the list is empty or indices are invalid/out of bounds.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def validate_indices(s_idx, e_idx, list_len):\n        \"\"\"\n        Validates if the provided indices are within bounds and form a valid range.\n        Returns True for valid indices, False otherwise.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not (0 <= s_idx < list_len and 0 <= e_idx < list_len):\n            return False\n        if s_idx > e_idx:\n            return False\n        return True\n\n    def calculate_sum(nums_list, s_idx, e_idx):\n        \"\"\"\n        Performs the actual sum calculation for the specified range.\n        Assumes indices are already validated.\n        \"\"\"\n        return sum(nums_list[s_idx : e_idx + 1])\n\n    list_length = len(numbers_list)\n\n    if list_length == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    if not validate_indices(start_index, end_index, list_length):\n        return 0\n\n    return calculate_sum(numbers_list, start_index, end_index)"}
