{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(sorted_array, n, element):\n    # An empty array cannot have a majority element.\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Find the index of the first occurrence of the element using binary search.\n    first_occurrence_idx = -1\n    low = 0\n    high = n - 1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if sorted_array[mid] == element:\n            first_occurrence_idx = mid\n            high = mid - 1  # Search for an earlier occurrence in the left half\n        elif sorted_array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n\n    # If the element is not found, it cannot be a majority element.\n    if first_occurrence_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    # Find the index of the last occurrence of the element using binary search.\n    last_occurrence_idx = -1\n    low = 0\n    high = n - 1\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if sorted_array[mid] == element:\n            last_occurrence_idx = mid\n            low = mid + 1  # Search for a later occurrence in the right half\n        elif sorted_array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n\n    # Calculate the count of occurrences.\n    count = last_occurrence_idx - first_occurrence_idx + 1\n\n    # Determine the majority threshold (more than n/2 times).\n    majority_threshold = n // 2\n\n    # Check if the count exceeds the majority threshold.\n    return count > majority_threshold"}
