{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even-positioned bits (0, 2, 4, 6, etc.) to 1 in the given integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    mask = 0\n    # Iterate through bit positions up to the number's highest set bit.\n    # For number = 0, bit_length() is 0, so the loop range is empty and mask remains 0,\n    # resulting in 0 | 0 = 0, which is correct for input 0.\n    for i in range(number.bit_length()):\n        if i % 2 == 0:\n            mask |= (1 << i)\n            \n    # Use a bitwise OR operation to set all even-positioned bits to 1.\n    # Bits at odd positions remain unchanged, as specified in the design.\n    return number | mask"}
