{"task_id": "Mbpp/252", "solution": "import math\nfrom typing import Union, Tuple\n\ndef convert(input_num: Union[int, float, complex]) -> Tuple[float, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a complex number or real number to polar coordinates (magnitude, angle).\n    The angle is returned in radians.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Ensure the input is treated as a complex number\n    z = complex(input_num)\n\n    # Calculate magnitude using Python's built-in abs() for complex numbers\n    magnitude = abs(z)\n\n    # Calculate angle using math.atan2(imaginary_part, real_part)\n    angle = math.atan2(z.imag, z.real)\n\n    return float(magnitude), float(angle)"}
