{"task_id": "Mbpp/259", "solution": "def maximize_elements(tuple1, tuple2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Compares two tuples of nested tuple pairs element-wise and returns a new tuple\n    containing the maximum of corresponding elements at each position.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        pair1 = tuple1[i]\n        pair2 = tuple2[i]\n        \n        # Element-wise maximization for the current pair\n        max_first = max(pair1[0], pair2[0])\n        max_second = max(pair1[1], pair2[1])\n        result.append((max_first, max_second))\n        \n    return tuple(result)"}
