{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "def validate(integer: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in the integer is less than or equal to the digit itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    if integer < 0:\n        integer = abs(integer)\n\n    # Dictionary to store the frequency of each digit\n    digit_frequencies = {}\n\n    # Convert the integer to a string to easily iterate over its digits\n    s_integer = str(integer)\n\n    # Count the frequency of each digit\n    for char_digit in s_integer:\n        digit = int(char_digit)\n        digit_frequencies[digit] = digit_frequencies.get(digit, 0) + 1\n\n    # Validate the frequencies\n    for digit, frequency in digit_frequencies.items():\n        # If the frequency of any digit is greater than the digit itself, return False\n        if frequency > digit:\n            return False\n\n    # If all digit frequencies are less than or equal to their respective digits, return True\n    return True"}
