{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "def find_lucas(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the n'th Lucas number using an iterative approach.\n    Raises ValueError if n is a negative integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Validate that n is a non-negative integer as per design requirements.\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    # Handle the base cases for the Lucas sequence.\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    # Perform iterative calculation for n > 1, starting with L(0) and L(1).\n    a, b = 2, 1\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        next_lucas = a + b\n        a = b\n        b = next_lucas\n\n    return b"}
