{"task_id": "Mbpp/395", "solution": "def first_non_repeating_character(input_string: str) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first non-repeated character in the given string.\n    Returns None if no such character exists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return None\n\n    # Helper function to count character frequencies\n    def _count_characters(s: str) -> dict[str, int]:\n        counts = {}\n        for char in s:\n            counts[char] = counts.get(char, 0) + 1\n        return counts\n\n    # Helper function to find the first non-repeated character\n    def _find_first_non_repeated(s: str, char_counts: dict[str, int]) -> str | None:\n        for char in s:\n            if char_counts[char] == 1:\n                return char\n        return None\n\n    char_counts = _count_characters(input_string)\n    return _find_first_non_repeated(input_string, char_counts)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/397", "solution": "def _sort_three_numbers(num1, num2, num3) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sort three numbers in ascending order.\"\"\"\n    numbers = [num1, num2, num3]\n    numbers.sort()\n    return numbers\n\ndef _get_middle_value(sorted_numbers: list) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Extract middle value from sorted list of three numbers.\"\"\"\n    return float(sorted_numbers[1])\n\ndef median_numbers(num1, num2, num3) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculate and return the median of three numbers.\"\"\"\n    sorted_nums = _sort_three_numbers(num1, num2, num3)\n    return _get_middle_value(sorted_nums)"}
