{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "import functools\n\n@functools.lru_cache(maxsize=None)\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum for n using f(n) = max((f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\n    Uses memoization for performance optimization.\"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return n\n\n    sum_of_parts = (\n        get_max_sum(n // 2) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 3) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 4) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 5)\n    )\n\n    return max(sum_of_parts, n)"}
