{"task_id": "Mbpp/437", "solution": "def remove_odd(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Remove characters at odd positions from input string.\n    Returns string containing only characters from even positions using 1-based indexing.\n    \"\"\"\n    filtered_chars = []\n    for i, char in enumerate(input_string):\n        # Using 1-based indexing, positions are i+1.\n        # Even positions mean (i+1) % 2 == 0, which simplifies to i % 2 == 1 for 0-based index i.\n        if (i + 1) % 2 == 0:\n            filtered_chars.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(filtered_chars)"}
