{"task_id": "Mbpp/462", "solution": "def combinations_list(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates all possible combinations (subsets) of elements from a given list.\n    The combinations are produced in binary counting order, including the empty set.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n    all_combinations = []\n\n    # Iterate from 0 to 2^n - 1 to generate all possible binary patterns\n    for i in range(2**n):\n        current_combination = []\n        # For each binary pattern, construct the corresponding combination\n        for j in range(n):\n            # Check if the j-th bit is set in the current binary number i\n            if (i >> j) & 1:\n                # If the bit is set, include the corresponding element from the input list\n                current_combination.append(input_list[j])\n        all_combinations.append(current_combination)\n\n    return all_combinations"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "def max_subarray_product(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Find maximum product of contiguous subarray.\n    Tracks both maximum and minimum products at each position to handle negative numbers effectively.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n\n    max_so_far = arr[0]\n    min_so_far = arr[0]\n    result = max_so_far\n\n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        curr = arr[i]\n        \n        # If current number is negative, swap max_so_far and min_so_far\n        # because a negative times a negative becomes positive (large)\n        if curr < 0:\n            max_so_far, min_so_far = min_so_far, max_so_far\n\n        max_so_far = max(curr, max_so_far * curr)\n        min_so_far = min(curr, min_so_far * curr)\n\n        result = max(result, max_so_far)\n\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/470", "solution": "def add_pairwise(input_tuple: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the pairwise sum of neighboring elements in the input tuple.\n    Returns a new tuple containing these sums.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(input_tuple) < 2:\n        return ()\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(input_tuple) - 1):\n        result.append(input_tuple[i] + input_tuple[i+1])\n    return tuple(result)"}
