{"task_id": "Mbpp/479", "solution": "def first_Digit(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first digit of a given number.\n    It handles both positive and negative numbers by using their absolute value.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Take the absolute value to handle negative numbers\n    abs_number = abs(number)\n    \n    # Convert the absolute number to a string\n    num_str = str(abs_number)\n    \n    # The first character of the string is the first digit\n    first_char = num_str[0]\n    \n    # Convert the character back to an integer and return\n    return int(first_char)"}
