{"task_id": "Mbpp/597", "solution": "def find_kth(array1: list[int], array2: list[int], k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the kth smallest element from two sorted arrays.\n    Uses a two-pointer approach to avoid merging the arrays, ensuring O(k) time complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    len1, len2 = len(array1), len(array2)\n    ptr1, ptr2 = 0, 0\n    kth_element = -1\n\n    for _ in range(k):\n        if ptr1 == len1:  # array1 is exhausted\n            kth_element = array2[ptr2]\n            ptr2 += 1\n        elif ptr2 == len2:  # array2 is exhausted\n            kth_element = array1[ptr1]\n            ptr1 += 1\n        elif array1[ptr1] <= array2[ptr2]:\n            kth_element = array1[ptr1]\n            ptr1 += 1\n        else:\n            kth_element = array2[ptr2]\n            ptr2 += 1\n            \n    return kth_element"}
