{"task_id": "Mbpp/602", "solution": "def first_repeated_char(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Find the first repeated character in a given string.\n\n    Args:\n        input_string (str): The string to analyze.\n\n    Returns:\n        str: The first character that appears more than once.\n    \"\"\"\n    seen_chars = set()\n    for char in input_string:\n        if char in seen_chars:\n            return char\n        seen_chars.add(char)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/599", "solution": "def sum_average(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum and average of the first n natural numbers.\n    Utilizes mathematical formulas for efficient computation.\n    \"\"\"\n    sum_val = n * (n + 1) // 2\n    average_val = sum_val / n\n    return (sum_val, average_val)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/598", "solution": "def armstrong_number(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given number is an Armstrong number.\n    An Armstrong number is equal to the sum of its own digits each raised to the power of the number of digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    original_number = number\n    num_str = str(number)\n    num_digits = len(num_str)\n    calculated_sum = 0\n\n    for digit_char in num_str:\n        digit = int(digit_char)\n        calculated_sum += digit ** num_digits\n\n    return calculated_sum == original_number"}
