{"task_id": "Mbpp/748", "solution": "def capital_words_spaces(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Inserts spaces between words starting with capital letters in a given string.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return \"\"\n\n    result_chars = []\n    for i, char in enumerate(input_string):\n        if i > 0 and char.isupper():\n            prev_char = input_string[i - 1]\n            # Insert a space if the current character is an uppercase letter\n            # and the previous character is not a space\n            # and the previous character is lowercase or a digit\n            if not prev_char.isspace() and (prev_char.islower() or prev_char.isdigit()):\n                result_chars.append(' ')\n        result_chars.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "def divisible_by_digits(startnum, endnum):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds numbers within a given range that are divisible by every digit they contain.\n    Numbers containing 0 are excluded.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def extract_digits(number):\n        \"\"\"Extracts individual digits from a number.\"\"\"\n        return [int(d) for d in str(number)]\n\n    def contains_zero(number):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a number contains the digit 0.\"\"\"\n        return '0' in str(number)\n\n    def is_divisible_by_all_digits(number):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a number is divisible by all its non-zero digits.\"\"\"\n        digits = extract_digits(number)\n        for digit in digits:\n            # The contains_zero check should already filter out numbers with 0\n            # but as a safeguard, explicit check ensures no ZeroDivisionError.\n            if digit == 0 or number % digit != 0:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    # Parameter validation is omitted as per instructions \"Do NOT add isinstance() checks or raise exceptions for edge cases\"\n    # and \"Do NOT call any helper that is not defined inline in your response\",\n    # which would imply defining validate_parameters inline, making the function too long.\n    # Assuming valid_parameters has already been called and passed, or inputs are always valid.\n\n    result = []\n    for num in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        if not contains_zero(num) and is_divisible_by_all_digits(num):\n            result.append(num)\n    return result"}
