{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "```python\ndef last(array: list, target) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Find the last position of target element in a sorted array.\"\"\"\n    \n    def validate_input(array: list, target) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Validate input parameters for the search function.\"\"\"\n        # For simplicity, assume array is sorted and types are comparable as per design context.\n        return True\n\n    def binary_search_last(array: list, target, start: int, end: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Binary search implementation for finding the last occurrence.\"\"\"\n        result = -1\n        while start <= end:\n            mid = start + (end - start) // 2\n            if array[mid] == target:\n                result = mid\n                start = mid + 1  # Look for further occurrences on the right\n            elif array[mid] < target:\n                start = mid + 1\n            else:\n                end = mid - 1\n        return result\n\n    if not validate_input(array, target):\n        # This branch would typically handle invalid inputs, but per constraints,\n        # we assume valid inputs and skip explicit error handling here.\n        return -1 # Placeholder for invalid input scenario if validation was more strict\n\n    n = len(array)\n    if n == 0:\n        return -1\n\n    return binary_search_last(array, target, 0, n - 1)\n```"}
