{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def _normalize_distance(distance: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Normalizes the rotation distance to be within the 0-31 range for 32-bit numbers.\"\"\"\n    return distance % 32\n\ndef _perform_rotation(number: int, normalized_distance: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Executes the core bit rotation logic for a 32-bit number.\"\"\"\n    max_bits = 32\n    # Perform the left shift, and OR with the bits that wrap around\n    return (number << normalized_distance) | (number >> (max_bits - normalized_distance))\n\ndef left_rotate(number: int, distance: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates the bits of a 32-bit integer to the left by a specified distance.\n    The rotation is circular, meaning bits shifted off one end reappear on the other.\n    \"\"\"\n    normalized_distance = _normalize_distance(distance)\n    rotated_value = _perform_rotation(number, normalized_distance)\n    \n    # Mask the result to ensure it stays within 32 bits, as Python integers have arbitrary precision.\n    return rotated_value & 0xFFFFFFFF"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/801", "solution": "def test_three_equal(a: int, b: int, c: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Count the number of equal values among three integers.\n\n    Args:\n        a (int): First integer\n        b (int): Second integer\n        c (int): Third integer\n\n    Returns:\n        int: Count of equal values (0, 2, or 3)\n    \"\"\"\n    if a == b and b == c:\n        return 3\n    elif a == b or a == c or b == c:\n        return 2\n    else:\n        return 0"}
