{"task_id": "Mbpp/805", "solution": "from typing import List, Union\n\ndef max_sum_list(input_lists: List[List[Union[int, float]]]) -> List[Union[int, float]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the list in a list of lists whose sum of elements is the highest.\n    In case of a tie, the first list encountered with the maximum sum is returned.\n    \"\"\"\n    sum_with_indices = []\n    for i, sublist in enumerate(input_lists):\n        sum_with_indices.append((sum(sublist), i))\n\n    # Find the tuple (max_sum, original_index) using lexicographical comparison for tie-breaking.\n    max_sum_info = max(sum_with_indices)\n\n    max_index = max_sum_info[1]\n    return input_lists[max_index]"}
